#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Isaac GR00T: Vision-Language-Action Models"
msgstr "Isaac GR00T: Vision-Language-Action Models"

msgid "GR00T architecture connecting image and language inputs to robot actions."
msgstr "Image와 language 입력을 robot action에 연결하는 GR00T architecture입니다."

msgid "What Do I Need for This Module?"
msgstr "이 Module에 필요한 준비물"

msgid ""
"Mostly theory with code examples. No additional hardware is required beyond a computer with the "
"`so101-workshop` container built."
msgstr ""
"Code 예시가 포함된 이론 중심 module입니다. `so101-workshop` container를 build한 computer 외에 추가 hardware는 필요하지 "
"않습니다."

msgid ""
"In this session, we'll explore the VLA model called NVIDIA Isaac GR00T, how it works, and see "
"examples of it in action."
msgstr "NVIDIA Isaac GR00T라는 VLA model의 원리와 실제 동작 예시를 살펴봅니다."

msgid "Learning Objectives"
msgstr "학습 목표"

msgid "By the end of this session, you'll be able to:"
msgstr "이 session을 마치면 다음을 수행할 수 있습니다."

msgid "**Explain** what vision-language-action models are and why they're powerful"
msgstr "Vision-Language-Action model의 개념과 강점 **설명**"

msgid "**Describe** the GR00T architecture and its components"
msgstr "GR00T architecture와 구성 요소 **설명**"

msgid "**Understand** how VLAs differ from traditional robot learning approaches"
msgstr "VLA와 기존 robot learning 접근의 차이 **이해**"

msgid "**Explain** how batch size, training steps, and action horizons affect the workflow"
msgstr "Batch size, training step, action horizon이 workflow에 미치는 영향 **설명**"

msgid ""
"**Design** a checkpoint-continuation experiment, separating optimizer state, learning-rate "
"schedules, and data sampling"
msgstr "Optimizer state, learning-rate schedule, data sampling을 구분한 checkpoint continuation 실험 **설계**"

msgid "What Is GR00T?"
msgstr "GR00T란?"

msgid ""
"[NVIDIA Isaac GR00T](https://developer.nvidia.com/isaac/gr00t) (Generalist Robot 00 Technology) "
"is a research initiative and development platform for developing general-purpose robot foundation"
" models and data pipelines to accelerate humanoid robotics research and development."
msgstr ""
"[NVIDIA Isaac GR00T](https://developer.nvidia.com/isaac/gr00t)(Generalist Robot 00 Technology)는 "
"범용 robot foundation model과 data pipeline을 개발해 humanoid robotics 연구·개발을 가속하는 연구 initiative이자 개발 "
"플랫폼입니다."

msgid "It provides:"
msgstr "다음 기능을 제공합니다."

msgid "**Pre-trained visual understanding** from large-scale data"
msgstr "대규모 data로 학습한 **Pre-trained visual understanding**"

msgid "**Language-conditioned behavior** for flexible task specification"
msgstr "유연한 task 지정을 위한 **Language-conditioned behavior**"

msgid "**Action generation** suitable for real-time robot control"
msgstr "실시간 robot 제어에 적합한 **Action generation**"

msgid "In this course, we'll use GR00T 1.7 models post-trained for the SO-101 robot."
msgstr "이 과정에서는 SO-101용으로 post-train한 GR00T 1.7 model을 사용합니다."

msgid "**Training time in this course**"
msgstr "**이 과정의 학습 시간**"

msgid ""
"Training time depends on hardware and run settings. Train your own policy or use a compatible "
"LeRobot GR00T 1.7 checkpoint supplied for your workshop. See [Datasets and Models](datasets-and-"
"models.md) for compatibility guidance."
msgstr ""
"학습 시간은 hardware와 실행 설정에 따라 달라집니다. 직접 policy를 학습하거나 workshop에 제공된 호환 가능한 LeRobot GR00T 1.7 "
"checkpoint를 사용하세요. 호환성은 [Datasets and Models](datasets-and-models.md)를 확인하세요."

msgid "What Is a Vision-Language-Action Model?"
msgstr "Vision-Language-Action Model이란?"

msgid ""
"**Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models** take visual input, robot state, and language instructions"
" and output low-level or mid-level actions for an embodied agent, such as a robot."
msgstr ""
"**Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models**는 시각 입력, robot state, language instruction을 받아 robot 같은 "
"embodied agent의 low-level 또는 mid-level action을 출력합니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Modular Pipelines and Learned Policies"
msgstr "Modular Pipelines and Learned Policies"

msgid ""
"A modular robot pipeline might estimate an object's pose, plan a motion, and send that plan to a "
"controller. A VLA learns a mapping from images, task text, and robot state to action targets. For"
" vial placement, the policy learns from examples of what the robot saw and did instead of "
"requiring a hand-written grasp-and-place plan for each observation."
msgstr ""
"Modular robot pipeline은 object pose 추정, motion planning, controller로 plan 전달을 순서대로 수행할 수 있습니다. "
"VLA는 image, task text, robot state에서 action target으로의 mapping을 학습합니다. Vial placement에서는 "
"observation마다 grasp-and-place plan을 직접 작성하는 대신, robot이 보고 수행한 예시로 policy를 학습합니다."

msgid ""
"Both approaches still depend on sensing, calibration, and reliable control. A learned policy also"
" depends on demonstration coverage: the instruction alone does not teach it how to recover from "
"an unfamiliar grasp."
msgstr ""
"두 방식 모두 sensing, calibration, 안정적인 control이 필요합니다. 학습 기반 policy에는 demonstration coverage도 중요합니다. "
"Instruction만으로는 익숙하지 않은 grasp에서 회복하는 방법을 배울 수 없습니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "The Data Pyramid"
msgstr "The Data Pyramid"

msgid ""
"Data pyramid: human videos and web data at the base, simulated and synthetic data in the middle, "
"and real-robot data at the top."
msgstr "Data pyramid: 아래는 human video와 web data, 중간은 simulation 및 synthetic data, 위는 실제 robot data입니다."

msgid ""
"The pyramid shows complementary data sources, not prescribed proportions. Our workshop focuses on"
" simulation and real-robot demonstrations for post-training."
msgstr ""
"Pyramid는 상호 보완적인 data source를 보여주며 고정 비율을 정하지 않습니다. 이 workshop은 post-training을 위한 simulation 및 실제"
" robot demonstration에 집중합니다."

msgid "Defining Terminology"
msgstr "용어 정리"

msgid "Read more about model weights, pre-training, post-training, fine-tuning, and inference"
msgstr "Model weight, pre-training, post-training, fine-tuning, inference 자세히 보기"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Model Weights and Parameters"
msgstr "Model Weights and Parameters"

msgid ""
"**Model weights**, also called **parameters**, are the learned numbers inside a neural network. "
"This course uses the two terms interchangeably. Training adjusts the weights; inference only "
"reads them. **Hyperparameters**, such as batch size and learning rate, are different: you choose "
"them before training, and they control how the weights are updated."
msgstr ""
"**Model weights** 또는 **parameters**는 neural network 안에서 학습되는 수치입니다. 이 과정에서는 두 표현을 같은 의미로 사용합니다. "
"Training은 weight를 조정하고 inference는 읽기만 합니다. Batch size나 learning rate 같은 **Hyperparameters**는 학습 "
"전에 선택하며 weight update 방식을 제어합니다."

msgid "Understanding VLA Training Stages"
msgstr "VLA 학습 단계 이해"

msgid ""
"VLA models are not trained in a single step. They go through distinct phases, each building on "
"the previous one."
msgstr "VLA는 한 단계로 학습되지 않습니다. 앞 단계의 결과를 기반으로 여러 단계를 거칩니다."

msgid ""
"Understanding these stages helps explain how a model progresses from broad world knowledge to "
"task-specific robot behavior, and why each phase matters for sim-to-real transfer."
msgstr ""
"이 단계를 이해하면 model이 폭넓은 세계 지식에서 특정 task의 robot 행동으로 발전하는 과정과 각 단계가 Sim-to-Real transfer에 중요한 이유를 알 "
"수 있습니다."

msgid ""
"**Pre-training** is the first and largest training phase. The model learns general "
"representations from internet-scale data, including images, text, video, and increasingly, robot "
"demonstrations."
msgstr ""
"**Pre-training**은 첫 번째이자 가장 큰 학습 단계입니다. Image, text, video와 점차 늘어나는 robot demonstration 등 "
"internet 규모 data에서 일반적인 representation을 학습합니다."

msgid ""
"The model develops reusable visual, language, and action representations before adaptation to "
"your specific robot task. Broad images, language, and human video contribute visual and language "
"knowledge; robot experience connects observations with actions. SO-101 demonstrations then supply"
" the details of this arm, camera setup, and vial-placement task. These are data roles, not fixed "
"dataset proportions or a universal training order."
msgstr ""
"특정 robot task에 적응하기 전에 재사용 가능한 visual, language, action representation을 만듭니다. 다양한 "
"image·language·human video는 시각과 언어 지식을 제공하고, robot 경험은 observation과 action을 연결합니다. SO-101 "
"demonstration은 arm, camera setup, vial-placement task의 세부 사항을 제공합니다. 이는 data의 역할을 설명하며 고정된 비율이나 "
"보편적인 학습 순서를 뜻하지 않습니다."

msgid ""
"**Post-training** is the umbrella term for everything that happens after pre-training to make a "
"general model useful for a specific robot, task, or environment."
msgstr "**Post-training**은 pre-training 이후 일반 model을 특정 robot, task, environment에 유용하게 만드는 과정을 통칭합니다."

msgid ""
"This is where a pretrained foundation model is adapted to a specific embodiment and task using "
"demonstrations that map observations and language instructions to robot actions. Post-training is"
" computationally intensive and typically requires several hours on GPU hardware."
msgstr ""
"Observation과 language instruction을 robot action에 대응시키는 demonstration으로 pretrained foundation "
"model을 특정 embodiment와 task에 맞춥니다. 연산량이 크며 일반적으로 GPU에서 수 시간이 필요합니다."

msgid ""
"This is the stage you run in this course: taking the pretrained GR00T 1.7 foundation model and "
"adapting it to SO-101 data collected in simulation."
msgstr "이 과정에서 수행하는 단계입니다. Pretrained GR00T 1.7 foundation model을 simulation에서 수집한 SO-101 data에 맞게 조정합니다."

msgid ""
"**Fine-tuning** is a specific form of post-training where you continue training on a smaller, "
"targeted dataset to improve performance in a specific setting."
msgstr "**Fine-tuning**은 더 작고 목적이 명확한 dataset으로 학습을 이어가 특정 조건의 성능을 개선하는 post-training 방식입니다."

msgid ""
"For example, after post-training on simulation data, you might fine-tune on a small set of real-"
"robot demonstrations to reduce the sim-to-real gap. Fine-tuning aims to preserve general "
"capabilities while adapting behavior to new conditions."
msgstr ""
"예를 들어 simulation data로 post-train한 뒤 소량의 실제 robot demonstration으로 fine-tune해 Sim-to-Real gap을 줄일 "
"수 있습니다. 일반 능력을 유지하면서 새로운 조건에 동작을 맞추는 것이 목표입니다."

msgid ""
"**Inference** is when the trained model runs in real time. It receives camera frames and a "
"language instruction, then outputs joint position commands."
msgstr ""
"**Inference**는 학습된 model을 실시간으로 실행하는 단계입니다. Camera frame과 language instruction을 받아 joint position"
" command를 출력합니다."

msgid ""
"No learning happens during inference because model weights are frozen. Speed matters here. "
"Techniques such as action chunking, where the model predicts multiple timesteps at once, reduce "
"forward passes and produce smoother motion. On modern GPU hardware, this supports real-time "
"closed-loop control."
msgstr ""
"Inference에서는 model weight가 고정되어 학습이 일어나지 않습니다. 한 번에 여러 timestep을 예측하는 action chunking은 forward "
"pass 수를 줄이고 motion을 부드럽게 합니다. 현대 GPU에서는 실시간 closed-loop control을 지원합니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Training and Inference"
msgstr "Training and Inference"

msgid ""
"Training changes selected model weights; inference uses the saved weights with new observations. "
"A **frozen** component still computes features, but its weights do not receive optimizer updates."
" The base recipe freezes vision and language; the optional vision-unfreezing experiment lets "
"visual features adapt to task images. More trainable parameters require more memory and can "
"overfit a small dataset, so judge the change through matched rollouts."
msgstr ""
"Training은 선택된 model weight를 바꾸고 inference는 새 observation에 저장된 weight를 사용합니다. **Frozen** "
"component도 feature를 계산하지만 optimizer update는 받지 않습니다. 기본 recipe는 vision과 language를 freeze하며, 선택적인 "
"vision-unfreezing 실험에서는 visual feature를 task image에 맞게 학습합니다. Trainable parameter가 늘면 memory가 더 "
"필요하고 작은 dataset에 overfit될 수 있으므로 같은 조건의 rollout으로 판단하세요."

msgid ""
"Pretrained weights initialize post-training, where demonstration targets and an optimizer update "
"selected components; inference uses the saved policy with fixed weights."
msgstr ""
"Pretrained weight로 post-training을 초기화하고 demonstration target과 optimizer로 선택한 component를 "
"update합니다. Inference는 저장된 policy의 고정 weight를 사용합니다."

msgid ""
"Post-training adapts selected weights to SO-101 demonstrations. Inference uses the resulting "
"checkpoint without updating its weights."
msgstr ""
"Post-training은 선택된 weight를 SO-101 demonstration에 맞춥니다. Inference는 결과 checkpoint를 weight update 없이"
" 사용합니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Architecture Overview"
msgstr "Architecture Overview"

msgid ""
"GR00T 1.7 conditions action generation on images, language, and robot state. Its vision-language "
"backbone is Cosmos-Reason2-2B, and its action head uses flow matching to generate action chunks. "
"See the [GR00T 1.7 model card](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-3B)."
msgstr ""
"GR00T 1.7은 image, language, robot state를 조건으로 action을 생성합니다. Vision-language backbone은 Cosmos-"
"Reason2-2B이며 action head는 flow matching으로 action chunk를 생성합니다. [GR00T 1.7 model "
"card](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-3B)를 확인하세요."

msgid ""
"The conceptual **System 2** role interprets images and language; the **System 1** role generates "
"actions from those features and the robot state. This terminology comes from the [GR00T dual-"
"system architecture](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14734). The controller applies returned actions, "
"then fresh observations close the loop. This schematic describes data flow; it does not imply "
"that the policy returns a human-readable plan."
msgstr ""
"개념적으로 **System 2**는 image와 language를 해석하고 **System 1**은 그 feature와 robot state로 action을 생성합니다. 이 "
"용어는 [GR00T dual-system architecture](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14734)에서 유래합니다. Controller가 "
"action을 적용하고 새 observation으로 loop를 닫습니다. 이 그림은 data flow를 설명하며 사람이 읽을 수 있는 plan을 반환한다는 뜻은 아닙니다."

msgid ""
"Images and language enter the GR00T vision-language backbone; its features and robot state "
"condition the action head, which returns action chunks for control and observation feedback."
msgstr ""
"Image와 language가 GR00T vision-language backbone으로 입력되고, 그 feature와 robot state를 조건으로 action head가"
" control 및 observation feedback용 action chunk를 반환합니다."

msgid ""
"Images, language, and joint state condition the next action chunk; new observations provide "
"feedback without changing model weights."
msgstr ""
"Image, language, joint state가 다음 action chunk의 조건이 됩니다. 새 observation은 model weight를 바꾸지 않고 "
"feedback을 제공합니다."

msgid ""
"The Cosmos-Reason2-2B backbone inside GR00T is different from the separate [Cosmos 3 video "
"augmentation demo](14-strategy3-cosmos.md). Here it supplies features for action prediction; the "
"later demo generates visual variations of recorded clips."
msgstr ""
"GR00T 내부의 Cosmos-Reason2-2B backbone은 별도의 [Cosmos 3 video augmentation "
"demo](14-strategy3-cosmos.md)와 다릅니다. 여기서는 action prediction용 feature를 제공하며, 뒤의 demo에서는 기록된 clip의 "
"시각적 variation을 생성합니다."

msgid "Key Components"
msgstr "주요 구성 요소"

msgid "Read more about the vision, language, and action components"
msgstr "Vision, language, action 구성 요소 자세히 보기"

msgid "**Vision Encoder**: Processes camera images into feature representations"
msgstr "**Vision Encoder**: Camera image를 feature representation으로 처리"

msgid "Supplies visual evidence about objects and their spatial relationships"
msgstr "Object와 공간적 관계에 관한 시각적 근거 제공"

msgid "May remain frozen or be trained in the workshop's optional experiment"
msgstr "Freeze하거나 workshop의 선택적 실험에서 학습 가능"

msgid "**Language Encoder**: Processes task instructions"
msgstr "**Language Encoder**: Task instruction 처리"

msgid "Maps natural language to task embeddings"
msgstr "자연어를 task embedding으로 mapping"

msgid "Conditions behavior on the instruction alongside visual observations"
msgstr "Visual observation과 함께 instruction으로 행동 조건 설정"

msgid "**Cross-Modal Fusion**: Combines vision and language"
msgstr "**Cross-Modal Fusion**: Vision과 language 결합"

msgid "Attention mechanisms to relate visual features to language"
msgstr "Attention으로 visual feature와 language 연결"

msgid "Grounds language concepts in visual observations"
msgstr "Language concept을 visual observation에 grounding"

msgid "**Action Decoder**: Generates robot actions"
msgstr "**Action Decoder**: Robot action 생성"

msgid "Conditioned on fused visual-language features"
msgstr "융합된 visual-language feature를 조건으로 사용"

msgid "Outputs appropriate action representation (joint positions, velocities, etc.)"
msgstr "Joint position, velocity 등 적절한 action representation 출력"

msgid "What Happens in One Step of GR00T Training?"
msgstr "GR00T Training 한 Step에서 일어나는 일"

msgid ""
"One **training step** is an optimizer update, not an episode or a robot movement. A batch "
"supplies observation/action windows; GR00T computes a loss and uses it to adjust trainable "
"weights."
msgstr ""
"**Training step**은 episode나 robot 움직임이 아니라 optimizer update 한 번입니다. Batch가 observation/action "
"window를 제공하고 GR00T가 loss를 계산해 trainable weight를 조정합니다."

msgid ""
"Sample windows, prepare action and noise targets, compute loss and gradients, then update "
"trainable weights."
msgstr "Window sampling, action 및 noise target 준비, loss와 gradient 계산, trainable weight update 순서로 진행합니다."

msgid ""
"Batch size counts windows; the training horizon sets targets per window; learning rate scales "
"optimizer updates. Frozen weights do not change."
msgstr ""
"Batch size는 window 수, training horizon은 window별 target 길이, learning rate는 optimizer update의 크기를 "
"정합니다. Frozen weight는 변하지 않습니다."

msgid ""
"The action head uses [flow "
"matching](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/policies/groot/groot_n1_7.py):"
" it learns a flow from noise toward demonstrated action chunks. The **training horizon** sets the"
" target window, starting at the sampled frame; the rollout horizon controls how many actions are "
"used during evaluation."
msgstr ""
"Action head는 [flow "
"matching](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/policies/groot/groot_n1_7.py)으로"
" noise에서 demonstration action chunk로 향하는 flow를 학습합니다. **Training horizon**은 sampled frame에서 시작하는 "
"target window를 정하고, rollout horizon은 평가에 사용할 action 수를 정합니다."

msgid ""
"Our verified sim-only and mixed HG-DAgger 20,000-step runs took about **12½ and 13½ hours**, "
"respectively, on a **single H100 GPU**. These times include checkpoint saving, but exclude "
"dataset preparation, upload, and evaluation. Training time varies with the recipe and "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"검증한 sim-only 및 mixed HG-DAgger 20,000-step run은 **H100 GPU 한 대**에서 각각 약 **12½시간과 13½시간**이 걸렸습니다. "
"Checkpoint 저장 시간은 포함하지만 dataset 준비, upload, 평가는 제외합니다. 시간은 recipe와 구현에 따라 달라집니다."

msgid "Reference: Post-Train Your Own Model"
msgstr "참고: 직접 Model Post-Training"

msgid ""
"Run in the same `so101-workshop` container used for recording. The commands below load a LeRobot "
"dataset by its Hugging Face repository ID. Stop the collection process before starting training."
msgstr ""
"Recording에 사용한 같은 `so101-workshop` container에서 실행합니다. 아래 명령은 Hugging Face repository ID로 LeRobot "
"dataset을 읽습니다. 학습 전에 수집 process를 종료하세요."

msgid ""
"**Upload** and **inspect** your dataset as described in [Teleoperating in Sim](08-simulation-"
"teleoperation.md#review-and-upload-collected-data)."
msgstr ""
"[Teleoperating in Sim](08-simulation-teleoperation.md#review-and-upload-collected-data)에 따라 "
"dataset을 **upload하고 검토**합니다."

msgid "Inside the container, **authenticate** and **set** the run variables:"
msgstr "Container 안에서 **인증**하고 run variable을 **설정**합니다."

msgid ""
"Use your actual username and dataset. For [automated collection](08-simulation-teleoperation.md"
"#optional-automated-data-collection), set `DATASET_NAME=so101_auto_vials_newton` before defining "
"`DATASET`, `REPO_ID`, and `OUTPUT_DIR`. `REPO_ID` names the model repository; `OUTPUT_DIR` is "
"under the host-mounted `outputs/` directory. A dataset saved only under `datasets/` must be "
"uploaded before using the Hub-based command below."
msgstr ""
"실제 username과 dataset을 사용하세요. [자동 수집](08-simulation-teleoperation.md#optional-automated-data-"
"collection) data라면 `DATASET`, `REPO_ID`, `OUTPUT_DIR`을 정의하기 전에 "
"`DATASET_NAME=so101_auto_vials_newton`으로 설정합니다. `REPO_ID`는 model repository 이름이고 `OUTPUT_DIR`은 "
"host-mounted `outputs/` 아래입니다. `datasets/`에만 저장된 dataset은 아래 Hub 기반 명령 전에 upload해야 합니다."

msgid "**Run** single-GPU post-training with the suggested settings above:"
msgstr "위 권장 설정으로 single-GPU post-training을 **실행**합니다."

msgid ""
"This configuration uses 20,000 steps, checkpoints every 5,000 steps, image augmentation, BF16, "
"and Hub upload. Reduce batch size if GPU memory is insufficient. For local artifacts only, use "
"`--policy.push_to_hub=false`; for training without Weights & Biases, use `--wandb.enable=false`."
msgstr ""
"20,000 step, 5,000 step마다 checkpoint 저장, image augmentation, BF16, Hub upload를 사용합니다. GPU memory가"
" 부족하면 batch size를 줄이세요. Local artifact만 원하면 `--policy.push_to_hub=false`, Weights & Biases 없이 "
"학습하려면 `--wandb.enable=false`를 사용합니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Multi-GPU Training"
msgstr "Multi-GPU Training"

msgid "Show the alternative multi-GPU training command"
msgstr "대안인 Multi-GPU 학습 명령 보기"

msgid ""
"As an alternative for **step 3** on a machine with multiple visible GPUs, **run** Accelerate with"
" the same training settings. Choose either the single-GPU command or this command for a run. Use "
"a new `OUTPUT_DIR` for a separate training experiment."
msgstr ""
"여러 GPU가 보이는 machine에서는 **3단계** 대신 같은 설정으로 Accelerate를 **실행**할 수 있습니다. 한 run에서는 single-GPU 또는 이 명령"
" 중 하나를 선택하세요. 별도 실험에는 새 `OUTPUT_DIR`을 사용합니다."

msgid "Select the Trained Policy"
msgstr "학습한 Policy 선택"

msgid "After training finishes, **select** the uploaded model repository:"
msgstr "학습이 끝나면 upload한 model repository를 **선택**합니다."

msgid ""
"Alternatively, select a local `pretrained_model` directory under "
"`outputs/train/<user>/<model>/checkpoints/`. Use the directory containing the saved policy "
"configuration, weights, and processors, rather than the enclosing training run directory. This "
"local path also works when training with `--policy.push_to_hub=false`."
msgstr ""
"또는 `outputs/train/<user>/<model>/checkpoints/` 아래의 local `pretrained_model` directory를 선택합니다. 전체 "
"training run directory가 아니라 policy configuration, weight, processor가 들어 있는 directory를 사용하세요. "
"`--policy.push_to_hub=false`로 학습한 경우에도 사용할 수 있습니다."

msgid ""
"Local checkpoints must include configuration and processor artifacts, not just weights. See "
"[Checkpoint Compatibility](datasets-and-models.md#checkpoint-compatibility). Continue evaluation "
"in the same container terminal after training finishes. If you reopen the shell, set `MODEL_ID` "
"again; ordinary exported variables do not persist across shells."
msgstr ""
"Local checkpoint에는 weight뿐 아니라 configuration과 processor artifact도 필요합니다. [Checkpoint "
"Compatibility](datasets-and-models.md#checkpoint-compatibility)를 확인하세요. 학습 완료 후 같은 container "
"terminal에서 평가를 계속합니다. Shell을 다시 열었다면 일반 export 변수는 유지되지 않으므로 `MODEL_ID`를 다시 설정하세요."

msgid "Optional: Unfreeze the Vision Encoder"
msgstr "선택 사항: Vision Encoder Unfreeze"

msgid ""
"Use `--policy.tune_visual=true` to train the vision encoder, and `--policy.tune_llm=false` to "
"keep the language backbone frozen. Use `--policy.tune_visual=false` for a frozen-vision training "
"run. These flags control which model parameters training updates; they do not change inference "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"`--policy.tune_visual=true`로 vision encoder를 학습하고 `--policy.tune_llm=false`로 language backbone을 "
"freeze합니다. Frozen-vision run은 `--policy.tune_visual=false`를 사용합니다. 이 flag는 학습 중 update할 "
"parameter를 정하며 inference 설정을 바꾸지 않습니다."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The selected [94% simulation policy](datasets-and-models.md#vision-trainable-20k-sim-only-"
"reference) used vision trainable, language frozen, batch size 32, and a 32-step action window. "
"The example below starts a new run from the GR00T base using those choices. Consult the model "
"card for the full recorded recipe and benchmark conditions."
msgstr ""
"선택된 [94% simulation policy](datasets-and-models.md#vision-trainable-20k-sim-only-reference)는 "
"vision trainable, language frozen, batch size 32, 32-step action window를 사용했습니다. 아래 예시는 이 선택으로 "
"GR00T base에서 새 run을 시작합니다. 전체 recipe와 benchmark 조건은 model card를 확인하세요."

msgid "Show a vision-unfrozen training example"
msgstr "Vision-Unfrozen 학습 예시 보기"

msgid ""
"After setting `DATASET`, `DATASET_NAME`, and authenticating above, run this alternative single-"
"GPU experiment. Its separate model name and output directory let you keep the frozen-vision run "
"for comparison."
msgstr ""
"위에서 `DATASET`, `DATASET_NAME`을 설정하고 인증한 뒤 대안 single-GPU 실험을 실행합니다. 별도 model 이름과 output directory를"
" 사용해 frozen-vision run을 비교용으로 보존합니다."

msgid ""
"After training, select this model for evaluation with `export MODEL_ID=\"$VISION_REPO_ID\"`. Use "
"the evaluation lessons' 16-action rollout settings even though this example trains with a 32-step"
" window."
msgstr ""
"학습 후 `export MODEL_ID=\"$VISION_REPO_ID\"`로 평가할 model을 선택합니다. 이 예시의 학습 window는 32-step이지만 평가는 과정의"
" 16-action rollout 설정을 사용하세요."

msgid ""
"This example changes batch size and action window as well as vision training. To isolate the "
"effect of unfreezing, use batch size 32 and a 32-step window for both runs, keeping the dataset, "
"optimizer settings, update budget, and evaluation conditions the same. Unfreezing requires more "
"memory and is not guaranteed to improve performance."
msgstr ""
"이 예시는 vision 학습뿐 아니라 batch size와 action window도 바꿉니다. Unfreezing의 효과만 보려면 두 run 모두 batch size 32와"
" 32-step window를 사용하고 dataset, optimizer 설정, update 수, 평가 조건을 동일하게 유지하세요. Unfreezing에는 더 많은 "
"memory가 필요하며 성능 향상을 보장하지 않습니다."

msgid "Experiment Technique: Continue Training a Checkpoint"
msgstr "실험 방법: Checkpoint 학습 이어가기"

msgid ""
"You can train an existing policy further without repeating its earlier updates. For example, "
"start from a 50,000-step checkpoint and add 20,000 updates to explore what more training does. "
"Preserve the original checkpoint and compare both policies using the same evaluation conditions. "
"More training can improve behavior, leave it unchanged, or overfit the demonstrations."
msgstr ""
"기존 update를 반복하지 않고 policy를 더 학습할 수 있습니다. 예를 들어 50,000-step checkpoint에서 20,000 update를 추가해 효과를 "
"살펴봅니다. 원본 checkpoint를 보존하고 같은 평가 조건으로 비교하세요. 추가 학습은 개선, 변화 없음, overfitting 중 어느 결과로도 이어질 수 있습니다."

msgid "Read more about continuing a checkpoint, optimizer state, and data mixtures"
msgstr "Checkpoint continuation, Optimizer State, Data Mixture 자세히 보기"

msgid "Choose What to Restore"
msgstr "복원할 상태 선택"

msgid ""
"**Resume the training run:** restore weights, optimizer state, scheduler state, and the update "
"counter. This is useful for an interrupted run. It requires the full training checkpoint, "
"including training state, rather than only an exported policy. In this mode, `--steps=70000` is "
"the total target, so resuming at 50,000 leaves 20,000 updates. Inspect the restored learning-rate"
" schedule before extending a completed run; a rate that has decayed near zero may produce little "
"further learning."
msgstr ""
"**Training run resume:** Weight, optimizer state, scheduler state, update counter를 복원합니다. 중단된 "
"run에 적합하며 exported policy만이 아니라 training state를 포함한 전체 checkpoint가 필요합니다. `--steps=70000`은 전체 "
"목표이므로 50,000에서 재개하면 20,000 update가 남습니다. 완료된 run을 연장할 때는 learning-rate schedule을 확인하세요. 이미 0에 가깝게"
" 감소했다면 추가 학습 효과가 작을 수 있습니다."

msgid ""
"**Start a new fine-tuning run from saved weights:** load the policy and its saved processors, "
"then create a fresh optimizer and schedule. With `--resume=false`, `--steps=20000` means 20,000 "
"additional updates, counted from zero in the new run. This is useful for testing a new recipe or "
"introducing real demonstrations."
msgstr ""
"**저장 Weight로 새 Fine-Tuning run 시작:** Policy와 저장된 processor를 읽고 새 optimizer와 schedule을 만듭니다. "
"`--resume=false`에서 `--steps=20000`은 새 run의 0부터 세는 추가 update 20,000회를 뜻합니다. 새 recipe나 실제 "
"demonstration을 도입할 때 유용합니다."

msgid ""
"In LeRobot, `--policy.path` selects the trained policy and loads its configuration; the resolved "
"configuration records that location as `pretrained_path`. GR00T's `base_model_path` still "
"identifies the underlying foundation-model assets. Preserve the checkpoint's compatible base-"
"model revision, camera keys, joint order, action representation, horizons, and processors."
msgstr ""
"LeRobot에서 `--policy.path`는 학습된 policy와 configuration을 선택하며, resolved configuration에는 "
"`pretrained_path`로 기록됩니다. GR00T의 `base_model_path`는 기반 foundation-model asset을 지정합니다. 호환되는 base-"
"model revision, camera key, joint 순서, action representation, horizon, processor를 유지하세요."

msgid "Example: Add 20,000 Updates"
msgstr "예시: Update 20,000회 추가"

msgid ""
"Run inside the workshop container. Set `CHECKPOINT` to your actual LeRobot `pretrained_model` "
"directory, containing the weights, policy configuration, processors, and saved "
"`train_config.json`. The example reuses that training configuration and dataset, with a new "
"output directory and a fresh optimizer. Check that its dataset and base-model paths are "
"accessible in this container."
msgstr ""
"Workshop container에서 실행합니다. `CHECKPOINT`에 weight, policy configuration, processor, "
"`train_config.json`이 있는 실제 LeRobot `pretrained_model` directory를 지정하세요. 기존 training "
"configuration과 dataset을 재사용하되 output directory와 optimizer는 새로 만듭니다. Dataset과 base-model 경로가 "
"container에서 접근 가능한지 확인하세요."

msgid ""
"The example's `1e-5` peak learning rate and 5% warmup are experiment settings, not a proven "
"optimum. With this preset, `policy.max_steps` supplies the warmup calculation; the outer `steps` "
"sets the update budget. The new `020000` checkpoint represents 50,000 earlier updates plus 20,000"
" additional updates. Batch size, augmentation, and which model components are frozen come from "
"the saved configuration; review the resolved settings before training."
msgstr ""
"Peak learning rate `1e-5`와 warmup 5%는 실험 설정이며 검증된 최적값이 아닙니다. 이 preset에서는 `policy.max_steps`가 "
"warmup 계산에, 바깥쪽 `steps`가 update 수에 사용됩니다. 새 `020000` checkpoint는 이전 50,000회와 추가 20,000회 update를 "
"거친 결과입니다. Batch size, augmentation, frozen component는 저장된 configuration에서 가져오므로 실행 전에 resolved "
"setting을 확인하세요."

msgid "Example: Match the Gripper Mapping"
msgstr "예시: Gripper Mapping 맞추기"

msgid ""
"A gripper percentage can mean a different physical opening when its encoder calibration differs. "
"Collection and simulation inference share `utils/gripper_calibration.py`, with 1485 ticks as the "
"default. For a model known to have used the older 1531-tick span, add `--gripper_span_ticks 1531`"
" to the usual `lerobot_eval` command. Both observation and action conversions use that span; the "
"five arm coordinates stay unchanged. This override assumes the same jaw-angle zero."
msgstr ""
"Encoder calibration이 다르면 같은 gripper percent가 다른 실제 opening을 뜻할 수 있습니다. 수집과 simulation inference는 "
"기본 1485-tick의 `utils/gripper_calibration.py`를 공유합니다. 이전 1531-tick span으로 학습한 model임이 확인되면 일반 "
"`lerobot_eval` 명령에 `--gripper_span_ticks 1531`을 추가하세요. Observation과 action 변환 모두 이 span을 사용하고 5개 "
"arm 좌표는 그대로입니다. 같은 jaw-angle zero를 가정한 override입니다."

msgid ""
"A measured robot mapping can similarly translate gripper values without changing model weights. "
"Here is the calculation only; it does not move or connect a robot:"
msgstr "측정한 robot mapping으로도 weight를 바꾸지 않고 gripper 값을 변환할 수 있습니다. 아래는 계산만 수행하며 robot에 연결하거나 움직이지 않습니다."

msgid ""
"For deployment, this calculation belongs before policy state normalization and after action "
"decoding. The example is not automatically installed into `lerobot-rollout`. Measure the robot's "
"encoder span **and** physical jaw-angle zero in the same frame; retain the robot driver's limits."
" Matching gripper coordinates does not correct other arm offsets or establish real-task success."
msgstr ""
"배포에서는 policy state normalization 전과 action decoding 후에 이 계산을 적용합니다. 예시가 `lerobot-rollout`에 자동 "
"설치되지는 않습니다. 같은 frame에서 encoder span**과** 실제 jaw-angle zero를 측정하고 driver limit을 유지하세요. Gripper 좌표를"
" 맞추는 것으로 다른 arm offset이나 실제 task 성공까지 해결·입증되지는 않습니다."

msgid "Is a Fresh Optimizer Better?"
msgstr "새 Optimizer가 더 좋을까?"

msgid ""
"The model weights store learned behavior. Adam's optimizer state stores running estimates of "
"gradient direction and magnitude that guide future updates. Resetting those estimates preserves "
"the weights."
msgstr ""
"Model weight는 학습된 행동을 저장합니다. Adam optimizer state는 이후 update 방향을 정하는 gradient 방향과 크기의 이동 추정값을 "
"저장합니다. 이를 초기화해도 weight는 보존됩니다."

msgid ""
"A reset may help when moving from simulation-only data to a sim/real mixture because the gradient"
" distribution changes. It also discards potentially useful history and can make early updates "
"less stable. Keeping optimizer state can be useful when continuing the same objective and data. "
"Neither choice guarantees better performance."
msgstr ""
"Simulation-only에서 sim/real mixture로 바꾸면 gradient distribution이 달라져 reset이 도움이 될 수 있습니다. 반면 유용한 "
"이력을 잃고 초기 update가 불안정해질 수도 있습니다. 같은 objective와 data로 계속 학습할 때는 state 유지가 유용할 수 있습니다. 어느 쪽도 성능 향상을"
" 보장하지 않습니다."

msgid ""
"**An optimizer reset and a learning-rate restart are separate choices.** Continuing with a useful"
" learning rate after a schedule has decayed can matter even without resetting Adam. To test the "
"reset itself, start from identical weights and keep the sampled batches, trainable parameters, "
"update budget, and learning-rate schedule identical; change only whether optimizer state is "
"restored. Extra training plus a reset plus a different schedule tests the whole recipe, not the "
"reset alone."
msgstr ""
"**Optimizer reset과 learning-rate restart는 별개의 선택입니다.** Adam을 reset하지 않아도 감소한 learning rate를 다시 "
"유효한 값으로 쓰는 것이 중요할 수 있습니다. Reset 자체를 비교하려면 동일 weight에서 시작하고 batch, trainable parameter, update 수, "
"learning-rate schedule을 맞춘 뒤 optimizer state 복원 여부만 바꾸세요. 추가 학습·reset·schedule 변경을 함께 하면 recipe "
"전체를 평가하는 실험입니다."

msgid "Adding Real Data: Control the Sampling Ratio"
msgstr "실제 Data 추가: Sampling Ratio 제어"

msgid ""
"Two useful experiments are starting from the simulation-trained checkpoint and continuing on "
"mixed sim/real data, or starting from pretrained GR00T and using that mixture from the beginning."
" The first reuses task-specific learning; the second exposes the policy to real examples earlier."
" Account for the first stage's training cost and data exposure when comparing them. Continuing on"
" real data alone is a separate experiment and may overfit a small collection."
msgstr ""
"Simulation checkpoint에서 mixed sim/real data로 이어 학습하거나, pretrained GR00T에서 처음부터 mixture를 사용할 수 "
"있습니다. 전자는 task 학습을 재사용하고 후자는 실제 예시를 일찍 접합니다. 비교 시 첫 단계의 비용과 data 노출도 고려하세요. 실제 data만으로 이어 학습하는 것은"
" 별도 실험이며 작은 dataset에 overfit될 수 있습니다."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The sampling ratio controls how often training selects each source, independently of how many "
"demonstrations you store. At batch size 32, a 50% real / 50% sim ratio gives about 16 examples "
"from each source on average; 25% real gives about 8. A weighted sampler produces those "
"proportions over many draws, while a fixed batch composition can enforce exact counts."
msgstr ""
"Sampling ratio는 저장한 demonstration 수와 별개로 각 source를 뽑는 빈도를 정합니다. Batch size 32에서 real/sim 50%씩이면 "
"평균 약 16개씩, real 25%면 약 8개입니다. Weighted sampler는 많은 추출에 걸쳐 비율을 맞추고, 고정 batch 구성은 정확한 수를 강제할 수 "
"있습니다."

msgid ""
"For uniform sampling within each source, assign each eligible real training frame weight `p_real "
"/ N_real` and each eligible simulated frame weight `(1 - p_real) / N_sim`. Here, `N_real` and "
"`N_sim` count eligible training frames, not episodes. More real-data sampling revisits the "
"limited real demonstrations more often; it does not create new diversity. Log the observed "
"sampling proportions and monitor overfitting."
msgstr ""
"Source 내부 uniform sampling에서는 eligible real frame마다 `p_real / N_real`, simulation frame마다 `(1 - "
"p_real) / N_sim`의 weight를 줍니다. `N_real`과 `N_sim`은 episode가 아니라 학습 가능한 frame 수입니다. Real sampling을 "
"늘리면 제한된 실제 예시를 더 자주 보지만 새로운 다양성이 생기지는 않습니다. 실제 sampling 비율과 overfitting을 기록하세요."

msgid ""
"**Check the trainer before setting a ratio.** The LeRobot `v0.6.0` training path used by this "
"lesson shuffles eligible frames and does not expose a sim/real mixture-ratio flag. Its GR00T "
"`balance_dataset_weights` and `balance_trajectory_weights` fields are unused by this path. "
"Merging datasets alone therefore does not enforce a chosen ratio: longer episodes contribute more"
" frames. Explicit ratios require a trainer or sampler that supports source weighting and retains "
"each frame's source identity. The weights above describe that experiment design, not an "
"additional command-line option for the example."
msgstr ""
"**비율 설정 전에 Trainer를 확인하세요.** 이 실습의 LeRobot `v0.6.0` training path는 eligible frame을 shuffle하며 "
"sim/real mixture-ratio flag가 없습니다. GR00T의 `balance_dataset_weights`, "
"`balance_trajectory_weights`도 이 경로에서는 쓰지 않습니다. Dataset merge만으로 선택한 비율이 강제되지 않으며 긴 episode가 더 많은 "
"frame을 제공합니다. 명시적 비율에는 source별 weighting과 frame source identity를 지원하는 trainer 또는 sampler가 필요합니다. "
"위 weight는 실험 설계이며 예시의 추가 CLI 옵션이 아닙니다."

msgid "Make the Comparison Informative"
msgstr "의미 있는 비교 만들기"

msgid ""
"Keep some demonstrations aside for testing: never use them to train the model or calculate the "
"normalization statistics that scale its inputs and actions. Checking predictions against those "
"unseen demonstrations is called **held-out validation**. A **rollout test** instead lets the "
"model control the arm and measures whether it completes the task. These checks measure different "
"things; prediction error can improve while task success worsens, or vice versa."
msgstr ""
"일부 demonstration을 test용으로 남기고, 학습이나 입력·action normalization 통계 계산에도 사용하지 마세요. 보지 못한 "
"demonstration과 예측을 비교하는 것이 **held-out validation**입니다. **Rollout test**는 model이 arm을 제어해 task를 "
"완료하는지 측정합니다. 두 검사는 다른 것을 측정하므로 prediction error가 줄어도 task 성공은 나빠질 수 있으며 그 반대도 가능합니다."

msgid ""
"Compare the original checkpoint, a continuation with the same data and trainable components, and "
"the proposed change using the same test conditions. This control helps distinguish gains from "
"extra updates from gains due to unfreezing or adding real data. Change one factor at a time, "
"record total updates and sampled examples per source, and test sim-to-real claims on the real "
"task as well as in simulation."
msgstr ""
"원본 checkpoint, 같은 data와 trainable component로 이어 학습한 대조군, 제안 변경을 동일 조건으로 비교하세요. 추가 update의 효과와 "
"unfreezing 또는 real data의 효과를 구분하는 데 도움이 됩니다. 한 번에 한 요인을 바꾸고 전체 update 및 source별 sampled example "
"수를 기록하며, Sim-to-Real 주장은 실제 task에서도 검증하세요."

msgid ""
"For implementation details, see [LeRobot's training "
"configuration](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/configs/train.py) "
"and [frame "
"sampler](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/datasets/sampler.py). The"
" [Adam paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.6980) explains optimizer state, and [Sim-and-Real Co-"
"Training](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.24361) studies data-mixture choices. Continue with [Co-"
"Training in Practice](13-cotraining-practice.md#optional-collecting-real-demonstrations-with-"
"lerobot) for the workshop's data workflow."
msgstr ""
"구현은 [LeRobot training "
"configuration](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/configs/train.py)과 "
"[frame "
"sampler](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/datasets/sampler.py)를 "
"참고하세요. [Adam paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.6980)는 optimizer state를, [Sim-and-Real Co-"
"Training](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.24361)은 data-mixture 선택을 다룹니다. Workshop data workflow는 [Co-"
"Training in Practice](13-cotraining-practice.md#optional-collecting-real-demonstrations-with-"
"lerobot)로 이어집니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Overfitting"
msgstr "Overfitting"

msgid ""
"More training is not always better. If training loss keeps falling but performance on held-out "
"demonstrations or new rollout conditions gets worse, that can signal overfitting. Evaluate "
"checkpoints along the way rather than choosing by training loss alone. If gains stall, inspect "
"the failures and improve demonstration coverage before simply adding more steps."
msgstr ""
"학습을 많이 한다고 항상 좋아지는 것은 아닙니다. Training loss가 줄어도 held-out demonstration이나 새 rollout 조건의 성능이 나빠지면 "
"overfitting일 수 있습니다. Loss만으로 선택하지 말고 중간 checkpoint를 평가하세요. 개선이 멈추면 step을 늘리기 전에 실패를 분석하고 "
"demonstration coverage를 보완합니다."

msgid ""
"Watch how the policy stalls until the vial is moved into just the right position in the gripper. "
"Too little **domain randomization (DR) around the grasp** can leave a model relying on a narrow "
"set of familiar views."
msgstr ""
"Vial을 gripper의 정확히 익숙한 위치로 옮기기 전까지 policy가 멈추는 모습을 보세요. **Grasp 주변의 Domain Randomization (DR)**이 "
"부족하면 model이 좁은 범위의 익숙한 view에 의존할 수 있습니다."

msgid ""
"**Vary** vial positions and grasp angles in your demonstrations, then **test** positions you did "
"not train on. More episodes of the same grasp will not provide that missing variety."
msgstr ""
"Demonstration의 vial 위치와 grasp angle을 **다양하게** 하고 학습하지 않은 위치를 **시험**하세요. 같은 grasp의 episode만 늘려서는 "
"부족한 다양성을 채울 수 없습니다."

msgid "Key Takeaways"
msgstr "핵심 내용"

msgid ""
"**Start in distribution.** For best results, use a robot starting pose represented in the "
"checkpoint’s training dataset, including gripper opening. Check the actual demonstrations rather "
"than assuming the default home pose matches. An unfamiliar start changes the camera views and "
"robot state, and can cause failures even with a well-trained policy."
msgstr ""
"**Distribution 안에서 시작하세요.** Gripper opening을 포함해 checkpoint의 training dataset에 나타나는 starting "
"pose를 사용합니다. 기본 home pose가 맞다고 가정하지 말고 실제 demonstration을 확인하세요. 익숙하지 않은 시작은 camera view와 robot "
"state를 바꾸므로 잘 학습된 policy도 실패할 수 있습니다."

msgid ""
"GR00T uses a **System 2** vision-language backbone to interpret images and instructions, and a "
"**System 1** action head to generate action chunks conditioned on those features and the robot "
"state."
msgstr ""
"GR00T는 **System 2** vision-language backbone으로 image와 instruction을 해석하고, **System 1** action "
"head로 그 feature와 robot state를 조건으로 action chunk를 생성합니다."

msgid "VLA models combine vision, language, and action in a unified architecture"
msgstr "VLA는 하나의 architecture에서 vision, language, action을 결합합니다."

msgid "GR00T provides pre-trained components for accelerated learning"
msgstr "GR00T는 학습을 가속하는 pretrained component를 제공합니다."

msgid "Action chunking provides smooth, temporally consistent control"
msgstr "Action chunking은 부드럽고 시간적으로 일관된 control을 제공합니다."

msgid "Pre-trained vision encoders enable visual generalization"
msgstr "Pretrained vision encoder는 visual generalization을 지원합니다."

msgid "Suggested Training Hyperparameters"
msgstr "권장 Training Hyperparameters"

msgid ""
"The values below are used in this lesson's commands. **Treat them as suggested starting points**,"
" not an optimized configuration or a guarantee of success. Dataset quality, task variation, and "
"GPU capacity can require different settings. The older AnchorBench comparison has its own "
"training recipe; do not mix its settings with this GR00T 1.7 example."
msgstr ""
"아래 값은 이 실습 명령에 사용됩니다. **권장 시작점으로 사용하세요.** 최적값이나 성공 보장은 아닙니다. Data 품질, task variation, GPU 용량에 따라 "
"달라질 수 있습니다. 이전 AnchorBench 비교는 별도 recipe이므로 GR00T 1.7 예시와 섞지 마세요."

msgid "Training parameter reference"
msgstr "Training Parameter 참고"

msgid ""
"The preset defaults and horizon limits above are checked against [LeRobot's GR00T "
"configuration](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/policies/groot/configuration_groot.py)"
" and [policy "
"implementation](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/policies/groot/modeling_groot.py)."
" Effective batch size follows the [pinned training "
"loop](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/scripts/lerobot_train.py). "
"Record the resolved optimizer and scheduler settings rather than inferring every default from the"
" command line."
msgstr ""
"Preset 기본값과 horizon limit은 [LeRobot GR00T "
"configuration](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/policies/groot/configuration_groot.py)과"
" [policy "
"implementation](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/policies/groot/modeling_groot.py)을"
" 확인했습니다. Effective batch size는 [고정된 training "
"loop](https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot/blob/v0.6.0/src/lerobot/scripts/lerobot_train.py)를 "
"따릅니다. CLI만으로 모든 기본값을 추정하지 말고 resolved optimizer와 scheduler 설정을 기록하세요."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Action Space and Control"
msgstr "Action Space and Control"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "Action Representations"
msgstr "Action Representations"

msgid "Compare joint actions, end-effector actions, and action chunking"
msgstr "Joint action, End-Effector action, Action Chunking 비교"

msgid "GR00T supports several action representations:"
msgstr "GR00T는 여러 action representation을 지원합니다."

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "**Joint Position Actions**"
msgstr "**Joint Position Actions**"

msgid "Direct control over robot configuration"
msgstr "Robot configuration 직접 제어"

msgid "Requires learning full arm coordination"
msgstr "전체 arm의 협응 학습 필요"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "**End-Effector Actions**"
msgstr "**End-Effector Actions**"

msgid "Inverse kinematics computes joint commands"
msgstr "Inverse kinematics로 joint command 계산"

msgid "Abstracts away arm configuration"
msgstr "Arm configuration을 추상화"

#. Reviewed: retain original technical label, identifier, source title, or existing Korean.
msgid "**Action Chunking**"
msgstr "**Action Chunking**"

msgid "Predict multiple future actions at once"
msgstr "여러 미래 action을 한 번에 예측"

msgid "Smoother execution, temporal consistency"
msgstr "더 부드러운 실행과 시간적 일관성"

msgid ""
"In this course, we use **joint position actions with action chunking**. Arm actions are "
"**relative** to the observed joint positions."
msgstr ""
"이 과정은 **joint position actions with action chunking**을 사용합니다. Arm action은 관측된 joint position에 대한 "
"**relative** 값입니다."

msgid "Prediction and Execution Lengths"
msgstr "Prediction과 Execution 길이"

msgid ""
"The **training chunk** describes the future action targets associated with an observation. The "
"**rollout horizon** describes how much of a predicted sequence is used before requesting another "
"chunk."
msgstr ""
"**Training chunk**는 observation에 대응하는 미래 action target을, **rollout horizon**은 다음 chunk 요청 전에 사용하는"
" 예측 sequence 길이를 나타냅니다."

msgid ""
"**Real-time chunking (RTC)** helps join consecutive action chunks while accounting for prediction"
" delay."
msgstr "**Real-time chunking (RTC)**은 prediction delay를 고려해 연속 action chunk를 연결하도록 돕습니다."

msgid ""
"Use a **16-action rollout horizon** throughout this workshop, including for the [selected "
"policies](datasets-and-models.md#current-model-selection) and the optional vision-unfrozen "
"training example."
msgstr ""
"[선택된 policy](datasets-and-models.md#current-model-selection)와 선택적 vision-unfrozen 예시를 포함해 "
"workshop 전체에서 **16-action rollout horizon**을 사용하세요."

msgid "Explore the Training and Inference Loops"
msgstr "Training과 Inference Loop 살펴보기"

msgid ""
"Adjust these diagrams to see the relationships. They are teaching illustrations, not a training "
"run or robot controller. The calculations assume the example's 16-step training window and no "
"gradient accumulation. The rollout timeline uses the workshop's nominal 30 Hz control rate and "
"excludes inference and network delays."
msgstr ""
"그림을 조절해 관계를 살펴보세요. 실제 training run이나 robot controller가 아닌 교육용 illustration입니다. 계산은 예시의 16-step "
"training window와 gradient accumulation 없음에 기반합니다. Rollout timeline은 기준 30 Hz를 사용하며 inference 및 "
"network delay는 제외합니다."

msgid "Resources"
msgstr "참고 자료"

msgid ""
"[NVIDIA Isaac GR00T GitHub](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T) — Source code, model weights, "
"and documentation"
msgstr "[NVIDIA Isaac GR00T GitHub](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T) — Source code, model weight, 문서"

msgid ""
"[Isaac-GR00T FAQ: Improving Policies](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/FAQ.md) — "
"Policy-improvement and troubleshooting guidance from the GR00T repository"
msgstr ""
"[Isaac-GR00T FAQ: Improving Policies](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T/blob/main/FAQ.md) — "
"GR00T repository의 policy 개선 및 troubleshooting 안내"

msgid "What's Next?"
msgstr "다음 단계"

msgid ""
"Confirm the physical setup matches [Building the Workspace](05-building-workspace.md), then "
"continue to [Real Evaluation](12-real-evaluation.md)."
msgstr ""
"실물 구성이 [Building the Workspace](05-building-workspace.md)와 맞는지 확인하고 [Real Evaluation](12-real-"
"evaluation.md)로 이동하세요."

